│ Mode: Agent                                                                            │
│ Runtime: Local                                                                         │
│ Max loops: 60                                                                          │
│ Task: Adversarial verification of a draft report. Treats every finding as probably     │
│ wrong until independently reproduced, requires a control test for each, checks for     │
│ duplicates and for anything dropped from the raw notes, and returns CONFIRMED /        │
│ REFUTED / UNPROVEN with evidence.                                                      │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Take the draft apart                                                            │
│ Objective: Turn prose into a checkable list of claims.                                 │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. Read the draft report and list every distinct claim: what is asserted, against    │
│ which endpoint, with what evidence, and at what severity and proof level.              │
│   2. Separately read the raw notes and evidence from the assessment. List anything     │
│ supported there that does NOT appear in the draft - omissions are as serious as        │
│ errors.                                                                                │
│   3. Identify duplicates: the same underlying issue reported as several findings, or   │
│ one finding split across categories. Merge them and say so.                            │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Attempt to refute each claim                                                    │
│ Objective: Reproduce independently. Assume the claim is wrong.                         │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. For every claim, reproduce it yourself against the live target rather than        │
│ trusting the quoted evidence. Evidence in a draft may be stale, partial or misread.    │
│   2. REQUIRED for every access, bypass or authentication claim: run the CONTROL TEST - │
│ the identical request WITHOUT the credential, token, header or material said to be     │
│ responsible. If the result is unchanged, the claim is REFUTED: the resource was        │
│ already reachable. Report both results side by side.                                   │
│   3. For claimed code execution, require output of a chosen command returned by the    │
│ target. A payload that was sent, or an interesting error, is not execution.            │
│   4. For any claim resting on a component, version or advisory identifier, require     │
│ that it was executed against this target with the effect observed. Otherwise it is     │
│ UNPROVEN regardless of how plausible it is.                                            │
│   5. Where a claim is correct but overstated, say so precisely: confirm the part that  │
│ holds and refute the part that does not.                                               │
│   6. Check severity against what was actually demonstrated and against breadth - one   │
│ object or all, one account or every account.                                           │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Return a verdict per claim                                                      │
│ Objective: Evidence for every verdict, in both directions.                             │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. Assign each claim CONFIRMED, REFUTED or UNPROVEN.                                 │
│   2. CONFIRMED requires the request and response you obtained yourself, plus the       │
│ control result showing it does not occur without the material.                         │
│   3. REFUTED requires the evidence that disproves it - typically a control test        │
│ producing the same result, or a reproduction attempt that fails.                       │
│   4. UNPROVEN means you could not settle it: state exactly what additional access or   │
│ step would settle it.                                                                  │
│   5. Add any finding you confirmed that the draft omitted, with the same evidence      │
│ standard.                                                                              │
│   6. Give a corrected severity for every surviving finding, and list the merges you    │
│ performed.                                                                             │
│                                                                                        │
│                                                                                        │
╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

